Packaging workflow
------------------

The branch debian/latest holds the packaging; upstream is the branch
main, and each release has a tag X.Y.Z (the version in pyproject.toml).

The packages are for my own repository; the distribution in
debian/changelog is trixie (the suite sbuild builds for).

Build the release in debian/changelog:

  sbuild-local

It gets the orig tarball with uscan (debian/watch, git mode: it reads
the tags with git) and builds for trixie with sbuild. Or with gbp,
which makes the orig tarball from the tag (debian/gbp.conf):

  gbp buildpackage --git-builder="sbuild -d trixie"

New upstream release X.Y.Z:

  git checkout debian/latest
  git merge X.Y.Z
  dch -v X.Y.Z-1 -D trixie "New upstream release."
  git commit -am "new upstream release X.Y.Z"
  sbuild-local

The run-time dependencies are in debian/control, not taken from the
wheel (dh_python3 --no-guessing-deps): check them against
pyproject.toml at each new release. OpenSesame and PsychoPy are not in
Debian yet; add them to Depends when they are.

The InpOut32 DLLs are prebuilt Windows binaries without source (only
used on Windows). debian/copyright excludes them (Files-Excluded), so
uscan repacks the tarball without them; a tarball made from the git tag
still has them, and debian/rules removes them from the package. For an
upload to Debian, use the tarball of uscan.

 -- Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026
